Generating Documentation Drafts
Use these prompts to transform raw notes or code snippets into well-structured documentation drafts:

Basic Draft Creation:
"Generate a clear technical documentation draft for the following notes: [insert notes]. Format it in Markdown."

Code Comment Explanation:
"Explain the purpose and function of this code snippet for documentation: [insert code]."

Feature Overview Draft:
"Write a user-friendly feature overview section for the product based on: [insert feature details]."

Reviewing Documentation Quality
Use these prompts to review clarity, grammar, and style:

Clarity and Grammar Check:
"Review this documentation text for grammar and clarity issues and suggest improvements: [insert text]."

Simplify Technical Language:
"Rewrite the following paragraph to be more accessible for non-expert readers: [insert text]."

Style and Tone Suggestions:
"Suggest improvements to the tone and style to make this documentation more engaging: [insert text]."

Fetching and Using GitHub Updates
Prompts to integrate repository updates for maintaining accurate documentation:

Summarize Recent Changes:
"Provide a summary of the latest commits and issues in the GitHub repo [owner/repo] that affect documentation."

Highlight Important Updates:
"Identify key pull requests and issues that require documentation updates for the repo [owner/repo]."

Example API Usage
Generate Documentation

bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/generate \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
  "input_text": "This module handles user authentication including login and token refresh.",
  "target_format": "Markdown"
}'
Review Documentation

bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/review \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
  "doc_text": "To log in, input your username and password correctly. If you encounter errors, please retry or contact support."
}'
Fetch Updates for Repo

bash
curl "http://localhost:8000/fetch-updates?repo=owner/repo"
